<section aria-labelledby="why">
  <h2 id="why">What I believe</h2>
  <ul class="cards">
    <li><h3>Your data, under your control</h3><p>Sovereign data means you decide where your information lives and who can reach it. I favour your own equipment, or UK and European hosting you choose, over handing it to whoever is biggest.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Privacy and security from day one</h3><p>Security isn't a bolt-on. I build with the least access needed, encryption where it counts, and clear records of who holds what, so you can answer awkward questions with confidence.</p></li>
    <li><h3>People before products</h3><p>The best investment is usually in your team's skills, not another licence. I'd rather leave you confident with tools you understand than tied into an expensive platform you can't change.</p></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="services">
  <h2 id="services">What I do</h2>
  <ul class="cards cards--pairs">
    <li><h3>Automate the admin</h3><p>Find the repetitive tasks that eat your week, such as forms, emails, data entry and reporting, and make them run on their own.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Private AI</h3><p>Set up AI tools that keep sensitive information under your control, including options that run on your own equipment.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Open-source alternatives</h3><p>Recommend and set up well-supported open-source tools that cut licence costs and keep your data portable.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Privacy and security reviews</h3><p>A plain-English look at where your data lives, who can access it and what would happen if something went wrong, with practical steps to fix the gaps.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Skills and training</h3><p>Hands-on sessions and clear documentation that build your team's confidence, so you own what we build and aren't dependent on me or on any one supplier.</p></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="how">
  <h2 id="how">How I work</h2>
  <ul class="principles">
    <li><strong>Private by default.</strong> Your data stays yours, and I only use what the job needs.</li>
    <li><strong>Invest in people.</strong> Money spent on skills stays with your organisation. Money spent on licences leaves every year.</li>
    <li><strong>No lock-in.</strong> Open standards and open-source tools wherever they fit, so you can walk away at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Affordable.</strong> The simplest thing that works, not the most expensive.</li>
    <li><strong>Plain English.</strong> I bridge the gap between technical and non-technical people.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

